          "paragraph_id": "P1",
          "quote": "On Monday evening, Noam opened the school website on his family's computer. His class had already planned a book sale for a community library. He wanted to make friends with Eitan, the new boy, so he asked him to help with the display. Eitan's answer appeared a minute later: “Do it yourself.” Noam read the three words again. They sounded like an order. “He thinks he is better than me,” Noam told his brother. He felt his face grow hot. Instead of asking for an explanation, he started writing an angry answer, then stopped. Tomorrow, he decided, he would cancel their work together."
        }
